From 84c8613416404d40a596d0fcbc7f133fba44b613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fork Author <fork@example.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 15:59:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: meal queue improvements

- Add 'Add to Queue' to the recipe context menu, available from both the
  recipe list cards (desktop + mobile) and the individual recipe page
  action menu.
- Add an 'Add Random' button on the queue page (server-side random
  ordering via orderBy=random + paginationSeed; prefers recipes not
  already queued).
- Fix the 'Show eaten' toggle: the frontend sends the camelCase
  includeEaten query param (like the rest of the mealie API), but the
  bare FastAPI parameter only accepted include_eaten, so the flag was
  silently ignored and eaten items could never be shown. Added an
  explicit Query alias.
- Add 'Clear Eaten' (with confirmation dialog) backed by a new
  DELETE /api/households/meal-queue/eaten endpoint, registered before
  the dynamic /{item_id} route.
- Fix the stretched/overflowing recipe thumbnail on desktop: the image
  now lives in a fixed 125x125 container using the small image size
  (RecipeCardImage enforces min-height 125, which previously overflowed
  the 60px slot).
- Queue entries now link to their recipe: clicking the thumbnail or the
  recipe name navigates to /g/{groupSlug}/r/{slug}.
- Integration test covering includeEaten, clear-eaten, and recipe slug
  presence for linking.
